<title>SOUTH KOREA: Kia union returning to work on Saturday.</title>
<headline>Kia union returning to work on Saturday.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union workers at South Korea's Kia Motors Corp will return to work on Saturday after joining nationwide strikes to protest the passage of a controversial labour law, a union spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The official said it was not clear if the work stoppages would resume at a later date.  </p>
<p>&quot;About 18,300 workers will return to work on Saturday. At that time, we will decide on further strike plans,&quot; said the official, who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>No further details were available.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
